==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|en|sort the wheat from the chaff|winnow the wheat from the chaff|winnow grain from chaff}}

===Etymology===
Derived from Matthew 3:12.<ref>{{R:KJV|Matthew|3|12|passage={{...}} he will throughly purge his floor, and gather his wheat into the garner; but he will burn up the chaff with unquenchable fire.}}</ref>

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en|En-au-separate the wheat from the chaff.ogg|a=AU}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb|*}}

# {{lb|en|idiomatic|intransitive}} To [[select]] only that which is of [[value]].
#: {{syn|en|winnow}}
#* {{quote-web|1=en|date=2022-07-13|author=Rachel Cheung|work={{w|Vice Media|Vice}}|title=A Bored Chinese Housewife Spent Years Falsifying Russian History on Wikipedia|url=https://www.vice.com/en/article/pkgbwm/chinese-woman-fake-russian-history-wikipedia|text=As a punishment, {{w|Zhemao hoaxes|Zhemao}} and her affiliated accounts were suspended permanently. Most of her articles were deleted based on community consensus. Some [[Wikipedian]]s even wrote to experts, seeking help to '''separate the wheat from the chaff'''.}}

